# Parallax sketch tileset (pass 2). One char = one pixel; `.` is transparent.
# A piece is <wtiles> x <htiles> tiles; its rows are wtiles*tile characters wide.
# ridge-a, b, c, d in this order form one seamless 512 px strip from tile row 7 down.
tile 16
color 0 000003
color 1 000004
color 2 000005
color 3 000007
color 4 010008
color 5 01010a
color 6 01010c
color 7 01010d
color 8 01020f
color 9 020211
color a 020313
color b 030415
color c 030517
color d 040619
color e 05071b
color f 05081c
color g 06091e
color h 070b20
color i 080c22
color j 090e24
color k 0b0f26
color l 0c1128
color m 0d122a
color n 0e142c
color o 10162f
color p 111731
color q 121933
color r 141a35
color s 151c37
color t 161e39
color u 181f3b
color v 19213d
color w 1a2340
color x 1c2442

# Bleed (vertical parallax 0.15): every piece runs 2 tile rows past the room bottom (y 368 to 400), the foot colour.
piece ridge-a 8 18
